.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-payment-methods - Discover a merchant's accepted wallets/tokens (public, no login)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 payment-methods [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List a merchant's active payment methods: its active wallets, each with the
active tokens (and chains) it accepts.

.PP
Public — no login required. Identify the merchant with exactly one of --account
(all its active wallets) or --address (just that one wallet; accepts an @alias).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--account\fP=""
	Merchant account id — list all its active wallets

.PP
\fB-A\fP, \fB--address\fP=""
	A merchant wallet address (0x… or @alias) — list just that wallet

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for payment-methods


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 payment-methods --account 019e748b-…
  rail0 payment-methods --address 0xABCD…
  rail0 payment-methods --address @payee
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0(1)\fP
